WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.114 --> 00:00:02.735
Senzu Labs is raising its next round.

2
00:00:03.719 --> 00:00:06.706
Bulma is leading an SPV into it,
and bringing her own investors.

3
00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:08.500
She sets up the deal,

4
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:11.316
and an operations team approves
it before anyone sees it.

5
00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:15.078
She invites investors by link, and
a link can carry its own terms.

6
00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:19.755
One of them, Goku,

7
00:00:19.755 --> 00:00:23.354
confirms he's eligible and sees
the exact amount before committing.

8
00:00:23.908 --> 00:00:26.682
Only after an identity check and
signing does he see where to pay.

9
00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:29.803
Then the deal's valuation changes.

10
00:00:30.553 --> 00:00:34.209
Do not send money: your earlier payment
instructions are no longer valid.

11
00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:39.003
Goku sees what changed, confirms,
and gets new instructions.

12
00:00:39.603 --> 00:00:42.547
She sees every investor: the
step, and who it waits on.

13
00:00:44.693 --> 00:00:48.618
Behind the deal, that same operations
team copies the investor list into Goten.

14
00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:51.007
Goku pays, but leaves out the reference.

15
00:00:52.162 --> 00:00:55.278
Goten books a payment only when
its reference matches one investor.

16
00:00:55.278 --> 00:00:56.813
Anything else waits for a person.

17
00:00:58.869 --> 00:01:01.686
At the close, the team
runs the numbers in Goten:

18
00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:03.871
fees, refunds, and the amount to wire.

19
00:01:03.871 --> 00:01:06.975
If a total doesn't add up,
it shows no figures at all.

20
00:01:08.845 --> 00:01:13.100
Then the emails. "I paid on Monday.
Has it landed?" A passport for KYC.

21
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:13.879
A withdrawal.

22
00:01:15.003 --> 00:01:18.152
Trunks first finds the deal, the
investor and the ledger entry,

23
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:20.301
and drafts the reply
from a fixed template.

24
00:01:20.301 --> 00:01:22.000
A person approves it and sends it.

25
00:01:23.027 --> 00:01:25.679
New bank details, from an
address that only looks right?

26
00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:27.574
Trunks never applies them from an email.

27
00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.262
It holds the case for a
call-back and a second person.

28
00:01:31.662 --> 00:01:33.092
Years later, the exit.

29
00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:37.252
Hurdle, catch-up, carry: Goten
splits every pound, step by step.

30
00:01:39.762 --> 00:01:40.432
Vegeta.

31
00:01:41.632 --> 00:01:42.877
More modules on the way.
